Hallucination detection starts with a definition. An answer is unsupported when it asserts a claim that the permitted evidence does not justify. That is different from an answer that is incomplete, poorly phrased, or unhelpful.

{% trace-scenario title="Unsupported or merely incomplete?" prompt="An answer contains a correct conclusion but one claim has no retrieved evidence. How should it be classified?" outcome="Evaluate claims individually, preserve the evidence chain, and distinguish unsupported content from a useful answer that needs an explicit caveat." /%}

